Add a Wiki app view to agent-os-v8 frontend (Lit Web Components).

CONTEXT:
- Frontend: /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8/
- Bridge backend: localhost:3100 (will have /api/wiki/* endpoints soon)
- Wiki web mirror: http://localhost:8090 (Quartz, full static wiki)
- Wiki API: http://localhost:8093

READ FIRST:
- /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8/src/app.ts — root component, all @state() properties
- /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8/src/app-render.ts — main render() with view routing
- /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8/src/types.ts — TypeScript types
- /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8/src/views/ — existing view files (look at 1-2 for patterns)

TASK 1: Add wiki state to app.ts
In the root component, add:
```typescript
@state() wikiSearchQuery = '';
@state() wikiSearchResults: WikiPage[] = [];
@state() wikiCurrentPage: WikiPage | null = null;
@state() wikiStats: WikiStats | null = null;
@state() wikiView: 'home' | 'search' | 'page' | 'graph' = 'home';
```

Add types to types.ts:
```typescript
interface WikiPage {
  id: string;
  path: string;
  title: string;
  type: string;
  status?: string;
  summary?: string;
  tags: string[];
  project?: string;
  updated_at: string;
  word_count: number;
}

interface WikiStats {
  total_pages: number;
  by_type: Array<{ type: string; count: number }>;
  spaces: string[];
}
```

TASK 2: Create /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8/src/views/wiki.ts

The wiki view should have 4 sub-views:
1. **Home** — search bar (big, prominent), stats cards (total pages, by type), recent pages list
2. **Search results** — results list with type badges, snippets, click to open page
3. **Page view** — title, type+status badges, metadata (project/tags/dates), rendered markdown content (use a simple markdown-to-html converter or pre tag), backlinks panel
4. **External link** — "Open in full wiki" button that links to http://localhost:8090 (Quartz)

Keep it simple — use the same CSS patterns as other views (cards, badges, etc.).

Methods to add to the view:
- `wikiSearch(query)` → fetch `/api/wiki/search?q=...` from bridge
- `wikiLoadPage(id)` → fetch `/api/wiki/page/:id` from bridge
- `wikiLoadStats()` → fetch `/api/wiki/stats` from bridge

TASK 3: Add "Wiki" to the sidebar navigation
Find where the sidebar nav items are defined (likely in app-render.ts or a nav component).
Add: `{ id: 'wiki', label: 'Wiki', icon: '📚' }` to the nav items.
Wire it: clicking Wiki navigates to the wiki view.

TASK 4: Add wiki context badge to Projects view
In the projects view (find projects.ts or similar), for each project card, add a small badge showing "N wiki pages" if the project has wiki pages.
Fetch from `/api/wiki/pages?project=PROJECT_NAME&limit=1` to get count (or use a count endpoint if available).

DO NOT:
- Add React/Vue
- Change the build system
- Modify vite.config.ts
- Break existing views

After building, run: `cd /home/trajan/Projects/agent-os-v8 && npm run build 2>&1 | tail -10`

Report DONE/DONE_WITH_CONCERNS/BLOCKED/NEEDS_CONTEXT when complete.
